[s0l0!-header][h1]Single-line Comments[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

C++ introduced a double slash comment // as a way to comment single lines. Some C compilers also support this comment style.
[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="c" codeId="1617"]#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
  int x = 42; [b]//int for a whole number[/b]
    
  [b]//%d is replaced by x[/b]
  printf("%d", x);
    
  return 0;
}[/code]
[note]Adding comments to your code is good programming practice. It facilitates a clear understanding of the code for you and for others who read it.[/note]

